 34MG c  2005Ch66: {+209}Bi({+34}Mg,{+34}Mg'|g). E=76.4 MeV/nucleon radioactive 
 34MG2c  beam of {+34}Mg was produced by fragmentation of a 110-MeV/nucleon     
 34MG3c  {+48}Ca primary beam on a {+9}Be primary target and separated by the   
 34MG4c  A1900 fragment separator at NSCL, MSU. The secondary target was 980    
 34MG5c  mg/cm{+2} Bi. The |g rays were detected using an array of 24           
 34MG6c  position-sensitive trapezoidal NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,   
 34MG7c  and scattered-{+34}Mg|g-coin. Deduced cross sections for population of 
 34MG8c  excited states, reduced electric quadrupole transition probabilities   
 34MG9c  B(E2), and deformation parameters |b{-2}.                              
 34MG c  2001Iw07: {+208}Pb({+34}Mg,{+34}Mg'|g). E=44.9 MeV/nucleon radioactive 
 34MG2c  beam of {+34}Mg was produced by fragmentation of a 95-MeV/nucleon      
 34MG3c  {+40}Ar primary beam on a {+9}Be primary target and separated by the   
 34MG4c  RIKEN RIPS fragment separator. The secondary target was 693 mg/cm{+2}  
 34MG5c  Pb. The |g rays were detected using a granular array of 66 NaI(Tl)     
 34MG6c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, and scattered-{+34}Mg|g-coin. Deduced    
 34MG7c  cross sections for population of excited states and B(E2). Also see    
 34MG8c  2002Mo35.                                                              
 34MG c  1999Pr09: {+197}Au({+34}Mg,{+34}Mg'|g). E=50.6 MeV/nucleon radioactive 
 34MG2c  beam of {+34}Mg was produced by fragmentation of an 80-MeV/nucleon     
 34MG3c  {+48}Ar primary beam on a {+9}Be primary target and separated by the   
 34MG4c  A1200 fragment separator at NSCL, MSU. The secondary target was        
 34MG5c  702-mg/cm{+2} Au. Beams passing through the target were detected and   
 34MG6c  stopped in a cylindrical fast-slow plastic phoswich detector located at
 34MG7c  zero degrees. The |g rays were detected using the NSCL NaI(Tl) array.  
 34MG8c  Measured E|g, I|g, and (scattered-{+34}Mg)|g-coin. Deduced cross       
 34MG9c  sections for population of excited states and B(E2). Also see 2002Gl01 
